    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers the day\u2019s highest efficiency score of 81.88. Facing a favorable 4.60 xERA matchup against Severino, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from an elite park factor (+16%) and his prime leadoff position (+10%). Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) presents a massive platoon edge against Alcantara (+14%) and provides critical speed leverage. While **Kyle Tucker** (69.90) and **Jackson Merrill** (66.44) remain high-floor staples, **Jacob Wilson** (69.51) is a sneaky play; his 16% park boost coupled with the pitcher's high xERA makes him a superior start to several of our higher-profile outfielders.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nasim Nunez**, whose 53.72 score fell just short of our utility threshold. While **Nasim Nunez** benefits from the Alcantara matchup and the pitcher's slow delivery\u2014which is a major green light for stolen bases\u2014his #9 spot in the order significantly suppressed his scoring potential compared to the middle-of-the-order production expected from **Josh Jung** or **Andy Pages**. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, as his return would instantly reshape our OF hierarchy and shift the efficiency landscape for the rest of the week.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos**, both of whom are facing elite arms (Gilbert and Chandler, respectively). **Sam Antonacci** manages a 46.73 score only because of his leadoff status and elite xwOBA metrics, but the -19% SP skill penalty against Gilbert makes him a candidate for mid-game substitution if the Waves fall into an early deficit. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.42) and **Brady House** (59.93) remain essential for our RBI production, though **Brady House** is the one to watch\u2014his score is bolstered by the potential for stolen bases against a slow-working Alcantara, a critical factor in maintaining our dominance in the scarcity category.",
